===Verbs===
Baliscano verbs have a single invariant form (the base form), unlike Mesogean languages with complex conjugations. All persons use the same form:
: ''yo kome, tu kome, el kome, nos kome, vos kome, los kome'' – "I eat, you eat, he eats, we eat, you (pl.) eat, they eat"

'''Copula:''' Baliscano has two copula verbs:
* ''ser'' – essential characteristics (''Yo soy profesor.'' "I am a teacher.")
* ''sta'' – temporary states (''Yo sta kansado.'' "I am tired.")

===Word order===
Basic word order is SVO:
: ''Yo kome pan.'' – "I eat bread."

Noun phrase order is Determiner-Noun-Adjective:
: ''la kasa grande'' – "the big house"

===Negation===
Negation is formed with ''no'' before the verb or TMA particle:
: ''Yo no kome.'' – "I don't eat."
: ''Yo no ya kome.'' – "I didn't eat."

Negative concord is standard:
: ''No ay nadi aki.'' – "There is no one here."

